{"id": "tea:tattvaprakasa-bhoja:1", "source": "src:tattvaprakasa-bhoja", "location": {"ref": "1"}, "paraphrase": "Victorious is Śambhu, the one pervasive, eternal, ever-risen, all-powerful, tranquil mass of consciousness, the sole seed of the world, who favours all beings.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "teachers": ["tch:bhoja"], "terms": ["trm:pati", "trm:siva"], "notes": "Opening verse; wording of the epithets recalled with moderate confidence.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tattvaprakasa-bhoja:ch.1", "source": "src:tattvaprakasa-bhoja", "location": {"ref": "ch.1"}, "paraphrase": "The categories are three: pati (Śiva), paśu (souls) and pāśa (bonds); Śiva's five acts — creation, maintenance, withdrawal, concealment and grace — are for the souls.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "teachers": ["tch:bhoja"], "concepts": ["cpt:pati-pasu-pasa", "cpt:five-acts-of-siva"], "notes": "Chapter- or work-level reference; exact verse not given.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tattvaprakasa-bhoja:ch.2", "source": "src:tattvaprakasa-bhoja", "location": {"ref": "ch.2"}, "paraphrase": "Souls are of three kinds: vijñānākalas, bound by mala alone; pralayākalas, bound by mala and karma; and sakalas, bound by mala, karma and māyā; each class is further divided by the degree to which its mala has ripened.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind"], "teachers": ["tch:bhoja"], "concepts": ["cpt:three-classes-of-souls"], "terms": ["trm:sakala", "trm:pralayakala", "trm:vijnanakala"], "notes": "Chapter- or work-level reference; exact verse not given.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tattvaprakasa-bhoja:ch.3", "source": "src:tattvaprakasa-bhoja", "location": {"ref": "ch.3"}, "paraphrase": "The bonds are mala, karma, māyā, and Śiva's concealing power (rodha-śakti), which is called a bond because it drives the others until the soul is ripe; some add the bond of bindu for souls in the pure worlds.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "teachers": ["tch:bhoja"], "concepts": ["cpt:five-malas"], "obstacles": ["obs:five-malas"], "terms": ["trm:tirobhava"], "notes": "Chapter- or work-level reference; exact verse not given. Enumeration low confidence.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
